{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T10:22:37.608Z","data":{"text":"I implemented task 2 and verified it end to end.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/core/vcs/sync-bridge.ts`** (new)\n- `syncBridge(vcs, defaultBranch, head, folderName, author)` returns the default branch when no landed tip shares history, else a bridge commit built with `commitTree(defaultBranch, defaultBranch, message, author, keptTips)`.\n- Keeps each `Osq-Head` tip once whose `mergeBase(head, tip)` exists and is not an ancestor of the default branch.\n- Message: `osq: <id> bridge <defaultBranch>` + blank line + `Osq-Change: <folder>`.\n- Tagged with the four \"Sync takes landed branch tips\" `@scenario` lines and `@adr 003`.\n\n**`src/core/vcs/sync-main.ts`**\n- Step 2 merges `syncBridge(...)` instead of always the default branch, inside the existing `try`, so bridge-build throws stop through `stopAfter`. Now 247 lines (≤250).\n\n**`tests/vcs-stacked-land.test.ts`** (new)\n- Three-change stack (`001` ← `002` ← `003`) archived via `approveSpec` + `runWatcherOnce`, landed in order with `landChange`.\n- Covers all four bridge scenarios, plus \"Stacked dependent after its dependency landed\" and \"Both add to one capability\".\n\nBoth verifications pass:\n- `node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/vcs-stacked-land.test.ts` → 3/3 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → typechecks, build, all tests, lint pass\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/165-stacked-land-keeps-history/.run/results/2.md`."}}
